NookBit @NOOKBIT_VERSION@ - Windows x64 test build
================================================

Quick start
1. Extract the entire ZIP to a writable folder.
2. Open NookBit-Release, then double-click nookbit.exe.
3. Keep the DLLs, qml, plugins and imagepacks beside the executable.
   Qt and development tools do not need to be installed separately.
4. If Windows reports a missing Microsoft Visual C++ runtime, run the included
   vc_redist.x64.exe, then start NookBit again.

First use
- File sorting: choose an organizing destination, add sample files, and inspect
  the preview before confirming a move. Undo is available for completed moves.
- Companion: open the Companion page and choose "Nmoo - Idle & Walk" to try the
  included character. No personal imported packs are included in this ZIP.
- Module management: select features, save, exit fully from the system tray,
  and launch again. Saving does not change currently running features.
- Closing the main window usually keeps NookBit running in the system tray.
  Choose the tray's Exit command to stop it completely.
- The application version is shown in Settings. The executable's Windows file
  properties and version.json report the same version.

Personal data and updates
The distribution does not include the developer's personal settings, rules,
history or pending files. Each Windows user has their own settings. Application
data is stored under %APPDATA%\NookBitProject\NookBit, and UI/module preferences
use Windows user settings. A fresh installation starts with the bundled defaults.
Close NookBit fully before replacing its application folder with an update.

Feedback
Report the version, the steps you followed, what you expected, and what happened.
A screenshot can help with visual issues. Do not send private files or personal
history unless they are actually needed to reproduce the issue.
